 "text": "Hi! How are you doing these days? You could try a small bike, like a 20-inch wheeler. They' easy to manoeuvre and fit in small spaces. No problem. You could also mount the bike outside the door, so it's ready to go as soon as you open it. You could also swap the door handle for one that swings out, so you don't have to reach over the bike. Okay, here's one more. You could build a little bike stand that folds away, or a coat hook with a little loop that the bike hooks onto. Then this is the one. It'll save you from every argument about who parked where.",
